IMPORT prelude

-- Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood Ordinance 1954 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "Reverend Mother Superior of the
-- Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood in Malaya" is and what a Gazette notification proves (ss 2(1), 4), what the
-- Ordinance empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)), how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 3), and whose rights the Ordinance leaves
-- alone (s 5).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/FMDMO1954.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The only amendment
-- annotation in the body is "[7/97]" under s 5. The Ordinance is dated 28 October 1954. Section numbers follow the body (s 1 short
-- title to s 5 saving); the arrangement at the top of the deposit is shifted by the PDF extraction (numbers out of line with their
-- headings) but carries the same five headings.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0234 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is five sections long, so the whole of it is in scope except the short title. For a person outside the Mission it
-- matters when buying, leasing or lending on the security of the Corporation's property (s 2(3)), and in checking that the
-- Corporation's deed was executed by the right person (ss 3, 4).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the preamble (the Mission's constitution at Guildford in 1935, its work at Tan Tock Seng Hospital and
-- Trafalgar Home, the intended Mount Alvernia Hospital), which recites but enacts nothing; the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and
-- Law of Property Act 1886, to which s 3(1) refers (whether a power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated
-- fact); how a Reverend Mother Superior is appointed, about which the Ordinance says nothing beyond s 4; the Corporation's internal
-- governance.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood Ordinance 1954 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and what the Gazette proves`

-- s 2(1): "The said Reverend Mother Mary Angela and her successors for the time being in office of the Reverend Mother Superior of the
-- Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood in Malaya, duly authorised and appointed as hereinafter provided, shall be a body
-- corporate", called the "Corporation", with the name "Reverend Mother Superior of the Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood
-- in Malaya", "perpetual succession" and a corporate seal.
-- s 4: "A notification in the Gazette of the appointment of any person to exercise the office of Reverend Mother Superior of the
-- Franciscan Missionaries of the Divine Motherhood in Malaya shall be conclusive evidence that such person was duly authorised to
-- exercise the said office."
--
-- The office is the Superior "in Malaya": a Superior of the congregation for some other region is not the Corporation. The 2020
-- Revised Edition keeps "Malaya". s 2(1) says "duly authorised and appointed as hereinafter provided", but nothing after s 2 provides
-- how a Superior is authorised or appointed; the only later provision touching appointment is s 4, which is a rule of evidence. So the
-- encoding takes "duly authorised and appointed" as a stated fact, and treats a Gazette notification as conclusively proving the
-- authorisation (s 4), but not as itself making the person the Superior "in Malaya" (an inference from the wording).
DECLARE Region IS ONE OF
    `Malaya`
    `another region`
    `no region -- not a Superior`

DECLARE Claimant HAS
    `is Reverend Mother Superior of the congregation for` IS A Region
    `is duly authorised and appointed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `appointment is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the region` IS A Region
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is Malaya` IF
    CONSIDER `the region`
    WHEN `Malaya` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `authorisation is conclusively proved` IF
    `the claimant`'s `appointment is notified in the Gazette`

GIVEN `the claimant` IS A Claimant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `holds the office that is the Corporation` IF
        `is Malaya` (`the claimant`'s `is Reverend Mother Superior of the congregation for`)
    AND (    `the claimant`'s `is duly authorised and appointed`
         OR `authorisation is conclusively proved` `the claimant`)

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as the Corporation thinks fit."
-- s 2(3): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as the Corporation shall think fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". Unlike the Bishop of Singapore Ordinance 1911 and the
-- Brothers of St. Gabriel Ordinance 1950, this Ordinance gives no express capacity to sue or be sued. Whether the general law supplies
-- one to a body corporate is outside the text and not encoded: the encoding answers only what THIS Ordinance grants.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell property`
    `mortgage property`
    `lease property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue in respect of its property`
    `borrow money without security`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `lease property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being or her attorney, duly authorised by power of attorney
-- deposited under section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886 and shall also be signed by the said Reverend Mother
-- Superior for the time being, or her attorney so authorised as aforesaid."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be taken as sufficient evidence that the seal was duly and properly affixed and that the same is the
-- lawful seal of the Corporation."
--
-- Three things must all be true: the seal, its affixing in the presence of the Superior or a deposited attorney, and the signature of
-- the Superior or a deposited attorney. An attorney whose power was never deposited does not qualify. The witness and the signer need
-- not be the same person on the words of s 3(1) (each limb says "the Reverend Mother Superior ... or her attorney"); that reading is
-- encoded. A former Superior is not the Superior "for the time being". The Ordinance provides no stand-in during a vacancy.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a former Reverend Mother Superior`
    `a sister with no power of attorney`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Superior or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Reverend Mother Superior for the time being` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence the seal was duly affixed` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Superior or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `5 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 5: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the right of the Government, all bodies politic and corporate, and all others except
-- such as are mentioned in this Ordinance, and those claiming by, from or under them."
GIVEN `is mentioned in the Ordinance` IS A BOOLEAN, `claims by, from or under a person mentioned` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is mentioned in the Ordinance` OR `claims by, from or under a person mentioned`
